-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 7, §7.5 מנהל חטיבה עליונה
-- The head of the upper division in a six-year school: when the principal
-- may appoint one, and the management reward the post carries.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `7.5 מנהל חטיבה עליונה`

@desc A six-year post-primary school, as far as section 7.5 asks about it.
DECLARE `six-year school` HAS
    `is a six-year post-primary school` IS A BOOLEAN
    `classes in the upper division`     IS A NUMBER
    `classes in the whole school`       IS A NUMBER

§§ `7.5.2 מינוי`

DECLARE `upper division appointment` IS ONE OF
    `appoint a deputy in charge of the upper division` HAS `within the existing management-hours standard` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_5__ssec_7_5_2/p1
GIVEN s IS A `six-year school`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal may appoint an upper division head` s IF
        s's `is a six-year post-primary school`
    AND s's `classes in the upper division` AT LEAST 9

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_5__ssec_7_5_2/p1
GIVEN s IS A `six-year school`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `upper division appointment`
DECIDE `appointing the head of the upper division` s IS
    IF `the principal may appoint an upper division head` s
    THEN PARTY `the school principal`
         MAY   `appoint a deputy in charge of the upper division` `within the standard`
               PROVIDED `within the standard`
    ELSE PARTY `the school principal`
         SHANT `appoint a deputy in charge of the upper division` `within the standard`
         LEST BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 7.5.2: the upper division has fewer than 9 classes"

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_5__ssec_7_5_2/p1
`what the deputy in charge of the upper division is called` MEANS "מנהל החטיבה העליונה"

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_5__ssec_7_5_2/p2 akn:chp_7__sec_7_5__ssec_7_5_2/p3 The section's source (אסמכתא): the circular it rests on.

§§ `7.5.6.1 גמול ניהול`

-- The management reward of a post-primary school principal is section
-- 7.6's, as a function of the number of classes; it is passed in as a
-- named input (`principal's reward`) until 7.6 is encoded.
@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_5__ssec_7_5_6_1__para_1
GIVEN s IS A `six-year school`
      `principal's reward` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER @desc the management reward section 7.6 gives a post-primary school principal for a school of the given number of classes
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `upper division head's management reward` s `principal's reward` IS
    85% TIMES `principal's reward` (`classes counted for the upper division head's reward` s)

@ref akn:chp_7__sec_7_5__ssec_7_5_6_1__para_2
GIVEN s IS A `six-year school`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `classes counted for the upper division head's reward` s IS
    s's `classes in the upper division`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_5__ssec_7_5_6_1__para_3 A pointer: how a maritime or agricultural school's classes are counted is section 7.3.6.1(1א), encoded there.

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_5__ssec_7_5_6_1/p1 akn:chp_7__sec_7_5__ssec_7_5_6_1/p2 akn:chp_7__sec_7_5__ssec_7_5_6_1/p3 The sources (אסמכתא) of section 7.5.6.1.

§§ `7.5.6.4 גמול נסיעות`

-- akn:chp_7__sec_7_5__ssec_7_5_6_4/p1 A pointer: travel reimbursement is section 7.3.6.3's (the deputy principal's), encoded there.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Examples (placeholder school).
`a six-year school with 10 upper classes of 24` MEANS
    `six-year school` WITH
        `is a six-year post-primary school` IS TRUE
        `classes in the upper division`     IS 10
        `classes in the whole school`       IS 24

#ASSERT `the principal may appoint an upper division head` `a six-year school with 10 upper classes of 24`
#ASSERT `classes counted for the upper division head's reward` `a six-year school with 10 upper classes of 24` EQUALS 10

-- A placeholder reward of 100 per class, NOT section 7.6's: the head of a
-- 10-class upper division gets 85% of a 10-class principal's reward.
#ASSERT `upper division head's management reward` `a six-year school with 10 upper classes of 24` (GIVEN n YIELD 100 TIMES n) EQUALS 850

#TRACE `appointing the head of the upper division` `a six-year school with 10 upper classes of 24` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `appoint a deputy in charge of the upper division` TRUE AT 1

§§ `Property checks`

-- The section's rules over their whole finite space: a school six-year or
-- not, with 0 to 20 upper-division classes of 0 to 30 in the whole school,
-- for a principal's reward of 100 a class (a placeholder that, like
-- section 7.6's, does not fall with classes).

`both booleans` MEANS LIST TRUE, FALSE

GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN, u IS A NUMBER, w IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `six-year school`
DECIDE `a checked school` x u w IS
    `six-year school` WITH
        `is a six-year post-primary school` IS x
        `classes in the upper division`     IS u
        `classes in the whole school`       IS w

-- 7.5.2: the principal may appoint a head exactly in a six-year school of
-- 9 upper classes or more, and more classes never take the permission
-- away. 7.5.6.1: the head's reward is 85% of a principal's on the upper
-- division's classes alone — the whole school's classes never change it —
-- so it is never more than that principal's, never negative, and never
-- falls with classes.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN x YIELD
                all (GIVEN u YIELD
                        all (GIVEN w YIELD
                                LET s MEANS `a checked school` x u w
                                    r MEANS `upper division head's management reward` s (GIVEN n YIELD 100 TIMES n)
                                IN      `the principal may appoint an upper division head` s EQUALS (x AND u AT LEAST 9)
                                    AND ((NOT `the principal may appoint an upper division head` s)
                                         OR `the principal may appoint an upper division head` (`a checked school` x (u PLUS 1) w))
                                    AND r EQUALS 85% TIMES (100 TIMES u)
                                    AND r EQUALS `upper division head's management reward` (`a checked school` x u 24) (GIVEN n YIELD 100 TIMES n)
                                    AND r AT MOST 100 TIMES u
                                    AND r AT LEAST 0
                                    AND r AT MOST `upper division head's management reward` (`a checked school` x (u PLUS 1) w) (GIVEN n YIELD 100 TIMES n))
                            (range 0 30))
                    (range 0 20))
            `both booleans`

-- With 8 upper classes the appointment is barred, and making it breaches.
#TRACE `appointing the head of the upper division` (`a checked school` TRUE 8 24) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `appoint a deputy in charge of the upper division` TRUE AT 1
